# Reference dumps and the toolchain — these live in a SIBLING folder, never in here.
# tools/check-gsc.ps1 resolves them via $PSScriptRoot\..\.. See docs/notes/test-pc-setup.md.
bocw-source/
bocw-source-main/
t9-src/
/reference/
ACTS/
# (anchored: an unanchored `reference/` also swallowed docs/reference/, which holds
#  tracked audit tables such as bocw-maps.md - noticed 2026-09-12)
*.tar.gz

# Compiler / injector build output
#
# ⚠ THE TEST FOR IGNORING A BINARY IS "CAN WE GET IT BACK", NOT "IS IT A BINARY".
#   Applying *.dll as a blanket rule cost this project the cwpatch
#   discord_game_sdk.dll on 2026-09-08 - see tools/README.md, "Irreplaceable
#   binaries". Classify before adding a pattern here:
#
#     rebuildable   our *.gscc, from src/      -> ignore. Correct.
#     re-fetchable  atian menu .gscc           -> ignore, but record URL + size.
#     NEITHER       cwpatch discord_game_sdk   -> ignore ONLY with an out-of-repo
#                                                 backup that is WRITTEN DOWN.
#
#   This repo is PUBLIC, so third-party binaries stay out of it either way -
#   which makes the out-of-repo backup the entire safety net, not a nicety.
*.gscc
*.exe
*.dll
*.vsix
bin/
obj/

# Local-only notes and anything account-shaped
*.local.json
*.local.md
secrets*

# generated by tools/dump-grep.sh — regenerable, findings live in docs/notes/dump-cross-check.md
dump-report.md

# Python bytecode cache from tools/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
